## TKT-00004 — Editing a listing kept the old photos

**2026-08-08** · Priority: Medium · Reported by David Teply · Branch `beta-0.0.1-tkt-00004`

### Symptom

"I uploaded an AI photo of myself, then a photo of the chainsaw, then I went to
edit it, removed my photo and added another photo of the chainsaw but it kept
the old photos."

### Root cause

**This was never a data bug.** The form has always sent the complete
replacement array, and the repository does a full column overwrite — the
database was correct the whole time, immediately.

What was stale was the *rendered page*. `/tools/[id]` is prerendered with
`export const revalidate = 3600` for SEO, and `revalidatePath` appeared nowhere
in the codebase. After saving, the owner is redirected straight back to that
listing and was served up-to-an-hour-old HTML still showing the photos they had
just removed. `router.refresh()` could not help: it clears the client Router
Cache, while the stale HTML lives in the server's Full Route Cache, which only
`revalidatePath` reaches.

Two things made it look more convincingly like a data bug than it was:

- Removed photos were never deleted from Storage, so their public URLs kept
  returning 200. The stale page rendered perfectly instead of showing broken
  images.
- `router.push()` and `router.refresh()` fired back to back without awaiting
  the navigation, so the refresh could land on the outgoing route.

### Changes

- **`apps/web/src/app/tools/[id]/actions.ts`** (new) — `revalidateTool(id)`
  server action calling `revalidatePath`. The first server action in the
  codebase. Only the detail route needs it; every other tool surface (`/`,
  `/search`, `/my-listings`) reads cookies or runs client-side and so was never
  statically cached.
- **`EditTool.tsx`** — awaits the save, revalidates the listing page, then
  navigates. The redundant `router.refresh()` is gone.
- **`ToolPhotoPicker.tsx`** — new `deleteToolPhotos()` removes photos an edit
  dropped, scoped strictly to the signing user's own `tools/<userId>/` prefix.
  Best-effort: the listing has already saved by then, so an orphaned file is
  wasted storage, not a failure the owner should have to act on.
- **`ToolPhotoPicker.tsx`** — the six-photo cap counted only newly picked
  files, so editing a listing that already had six photos accepted six more.
  It now takes `existingCount` and counts both.

### Correction to TKT-00003 — `supabase/migrations/0018_backfill_service_area_slug.sql`

Found by this ticket's end-to-end test, which edits a seeded listing.

Migration 0017 backfilled `location_point` but not `service_area_slug`: its
legacy branch only ran when `location_point IS NULL`, and every seeded listing
already had a point. All 29 pre-existing listings kept a NULL slug. Once the
form made City required, that left **every pre-existing listing un-editable** —
the select rendered empty, native validation blocked submit, and no error was
shown. Any edit to an existing listing would have failed silently in
production.

0018 backfills the slug by proximity to the nearest service area (verified to
agree exactly with each listing's stated city) and revises the trigger to
derive a slug whenever a row has a point but no area, so legacy rows heal on
any write.

### Verification

The important part of this ticket. `next dev` applies neither prerendering nor
`revalidate`, so an end-to-end test against the default dev server **passes
whether or not the fix is present**. Confirmed by removing `revalidateTool` and
running all four combinations:

| Environment | Fix | Result |
|---|---|---|
| production build | disabled | **fails** — old photo still rendered, reproducing the report |
| production build | enabled | passes |
| `next dev` | disabled | passes (vacuous) |
| `next dev` | enabled | passes (vacuous) |

So the spec is only meaningful against a production build. Added
`pnpm test:e2e:prod` (`PLAYWRIGHT_PROD=1`), which builds and serves before
running; the default `pnpm test:e2e` still uses the dev server for the other
specs. The requirement is documented at the top of the spec itself.

- `pnpm typecheck` — clean across all 7 packages.
- `apps/web` unit — 34/36. New: 3 `ToolPhotoPicker` tests for the cap, 3
  `ToolForm` tests for photo replacement ordering and `existingCount`
  plumbing. (The 2 failures are pre-existing — see below.)
- `packages/domain` — 21/21.
- Full end-to-end suite against a production build — 11/12.

### Pre-existing failures, untouched by this ticket

- `BugReportForm.test.tsx` — 2 tests expect a severity emoji (`🟡 Medium`) in
  the subject; the component emits `🐛 Toolshare bug report — Medium`. The
  component and its test were committed out of sync in `79552e0`. Not fixed
  here; needs a decision on which side is right.
- `e2e/invite-signup.spec.ts` — needs `check_invite_code`, which migration 0016
  deliberately omits locally. Addressed under TKT-00002.

### Notes for local runs

`e2e/tkt-00004-photo-edit.spec.ts` signs in as `elena.rodriguez`, not
`mike.harrison`, on purpose: the suite runs `fullyParallel`, and the TKT-00003
spec creates listings as Mike. Sharing one owner between the two made this test
flake when the full suite ran.

