## TKT-00003 — New tool listings not appearing in search

**2026-08-08** · Priority: High · Reported by MP, AT, NT · Branch `beta-0.0.1-tkt-00003` · Commit `79552e0`

### Symptom

A newly created listing was visible to its owner (My Listings, the listing's
own page, Bookings) but never appeared in search for anyone — including the
owner. Reported as "accessible on the owner's side, marked pending approval;
when approved is accessible to all users."

### Root cause

Two findings, one of which contradicts the report:

1. **There is no approval or moderation step in the product.** No `status`,
   `approval_status`, `is_approved` or equivalent column exists on `tools`, and
   none ever has. The "pending approval" the reporters saw was *booking* status
   on an unrelated surface. Nothing was ever waiting to be approved, so nothing
   would ever have released the listing into search.

2. **The real cause was a NULL geography.** `search_tools_nearby` filters on
   `ST_DWithin(t.location_point, …)`, but nothing in either app ever set
   `location_point` — the listing form's only location input was a free-text
   "Address / area" box, and no geocoder or trigger derived a point from it.
   `ST_DWithin(NULL, …)` evaluates to NULL, which is not TRUE, so every
   app-created row was silently dropped by the `WHERE` clause. Unlike the
   query's other three predicates, this one had no `IS NULL OR …` guard.

   The owner-side views that *did* work (`getToolsByOwner`, `getToolById`, the
   booking join) are all plain table queries with no geo predicate. That
   asymmetry is the entire bug: "works for the owner, invisible to everyone
   else" is the signature of "plain query works, RPC doesn't."

Confirmed against the production snapshot: of 31 tool rows, 29 carried a
geography value. The two exceptions were precisely the two listings created
through the app UI. Every searchable row came from `seed.sql`, which hand-writes
`ST_MakePoint` per tool.

A contributing factor: both the home and search pages wrapped their queries in
`.catch(() => [])`, so an RPC failure and a genuinely empty result rendered the
identical "No tools matched" state. That is a large part of why this survived
live testing — the page looked calm and simply reported no results.

### Changes

**Database** — `supabase/migrations/0017_tool_location.sql` (new)

- `service_areas` lookup table: 20 Phoenix-metro cities (Buckeye → Apache
  Junction, Florence → North Phoenix/Surprise) with centroid coordinates. The
  first eleven reuse the exact values `seed.sql` already used, so seeded and
  user-created listings in the same city land on the same point.
- `tools.service_area_slug` — an FK the trigger resolves exactly, rather than
  parsing free text back out of `address_display`.
- `set_tool_location()` — `BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE` trigger resolving
  `location_point` in three tiers: from the chosen service area; failing that,
  by matching legacy free-text `address_display` against known city names;
  failing that, Phoenix metro center. A coarse point is wrong by a few miles, a
  NULL point is invisible — the fallback guarantees a listing can never again
  disappear.
- Backfill of every existing `location_point IS NULL` row, including the two
  live listings that prompted the ticket.
- `search_tools_nearby` replaced, with two changes: a `location_point IS NULL OR`
  guard so a missing point can never again silently unpublish a listing, and
  `created_at DESC` added to the ordering — a brand-new listing has rating 0 and
  sorted behind every rated tool, which would have made the fix look ineffective.
  `search_path` pinning from migration 0015 re-applied (`CREATE OR REPLACE`
  resets function attributes).

**Listing form** — `apps/web/src/components/ToolForm.tsx`

- The free-text "Address / area" input is now a required **City** picker backed
  by `service_areas`. `address_display` is derived from the selection, so a
  listing can no longer display one city while being searchable in another.
- Location is city-level by design: only the city is shown publicly, never a
  street address.

**Shared packages**

- `ServiceArea` type; `service_area_slug` added to `Tool` and `CreateToolInput`
  (the latter previously made it impossible to type a location through at all).
- `getServiceAreas()` repository method, `toolKeys.serviceAreas()` key, and the
  `useServiceAreas` hook.

**Error visibility** — `apps/web/src/lib/loadTools.ts` (new)

- Replaces `.catch(() => [])` on the home and search pages. A failed query now
  logs server-side and renders a distinct "we couldn't load listings" message
  instead of masquerading as an empty result. Still degrades rather than
  throwing — one bad query shouldn't 500 the home page.

### Also fixed (pre-existing, outside the ticket)

Local sign-in was broken for all five demo accounts. `seed.sql` and
`scripts/supabase/sanitize-local.sql` inserted `auth.users` rows leaving
`confirmation_token`, `recovery_token`, `email_change_token_new` and
`email_change` NULL. Those columns are nullable with no default, but GoTrue
scans them into Go strings, so every login failed with a 500 —
`Database error querying schema` / `converting NULL to string is unsupported`.
Both files now write `''`. This was blocking any end-to-end test that signs in.

### Verification

- `pnpm typecheck` — clean across all 7 packages.
- `apps/web` unit suite — 30/30 passing, including 3 new `ToolForm` tests
  (`ToolForm.test.tsx`) covering the submitted service area, the derived city
  label, refusal to submit with no city, and preselection when editing.
- `packages/domain` — 21/21 passing (pricing and availability rules unchanged).
- `e2e/tkt-00003-search-visibility.spec.ts` (new) — creates a listing through
  the real form and asserts it appears in `/search`. This is the only test that
  exercises the RPC, and therefore the only one that covers the reported bug.
- Direct database probe — an app-shaped insert with no `location_point`, and a
  legacy free-text-only row, both resolve a point and return from
  `search_tools_nearby`.

### Notes for local runs

- E2E requires `E2E_OWNER_PASSWORD=localdev123`; the specs' default is the
  production demo password.
- `e2e/self-booking.spec.ts` needs `E2E_OWNED_TOOL_ID` set to a local tool id —
  its default is a production UUID that does not survive `supabase db reset`.
- `e2e/invite-signup.spec.ts` cannot pass locally: it needs `check_invite_code`,
  which migration 0016 deliberately omits from the local schema. Addressed under
  TKT-00002.

### Follow-up (not in scope)

`apps/mobile/app/tools/new.tsx` sends no location and hardcodes `category_id: 1`.
The new trigger's fallback makes mobile-created listings searchable, but they
will all land on metro center until the picker is added there too.
